# Hands and gestures

Draw a hand only when it helps explain the action, such as pressing the button on a smart plug. Keep it to simple shapes, like the rest of the person.

## What a hand does

A hand in a civica illustration does one of 2 jobs.

| Job | What it shows | Home Assistant example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Doing | An action, such as pressing, holding or turning | A finger pressing the button on a smart plug |
| Pointing | Where to look or which control to use | A finger touching a tile on a wall tablet |

A hand that points to a control must point to the right one. A hand that points near the wrong button teaches the wrong step.

## Gestures that need checking

Sign language, safety steps and accessibility gestures need checking by someone who knows the subject. Do not draw them from memory.

## Example

The [Characters example](illustration-characters.html#example) includes a hand pressing a smart plug button. The finger touches the plug button and nothing else.
